      "body": "The lack of privacy may not be a problem there. As long as the membership can be bought, a user wanting maximum privacy can acquire voting currency from an exchange or privacy-focused tool (like Coinjoin, Tornado cash, etc.), buy a membership, and vote privately. This brings only one extra step (buying membership) in comparison to a referendum without membership.\r\n\r\nIf we ever want to provide truly anonymous elections, we need to upgrade the voting mechanism with some Zero-Knowledge proofs or similar technology.",
